description:
The exact set of artifacts, engines, data and RNG state that produced a result. Analogous to a package-manager lockfile, and it is the mechanism that makes three otherwise-conflicting requirements compatible at once:

  * results are reproducible and auditable (BRIEF-2.2-d);
  * a submitted wet-lab observation triggers recalibration WITHOUT blocking or perturbing other users' in-flight jobs (BRIEF-2.4-b) - because every job pins its lockfile at submission, a new artifact version appearing mid-job is simply not visible to it;
  * host/dataset-specific model versions are selected at query time by a documented ladder (BRIEF-2.4-c) - the ladder runs ONCE, at pin time, and its outcome is recorded here rather than re-derived per query.

A lockfile is immutable and content-addressed. Replaying a job means loading its lockfile and re-running; if any digest is unavailable the replay fails loudly rather than substituting a newer artifact.
